# Content keyboard input: a focused page takes the scroll keys, delivered
# through the SAME key seam a real press uses (one description, two runners —
# the scenario's `key` verb now drives whatever holds focus, not just the
# omnibar). Network-dependent by design, like the other content receipts: the
# static lane routes http/https only, and the page needs real height to scroll.
# FRESH profile.
settle 30
key escape

# A page with real height, opened and made live.
open https://www.iana.org/
settle 50
act Toggle live content
settle 50
assert content-live
assert surface content
capture 01_page_top

# Clicking the page focuses it: the keys now belong to the page. The content
# surface is the right-hand half beside the canvas, and this lands in the
# whitespace between two sections (a press on a link would navigate instead).
click-at 700 355
settle 10
assert focus content

# The scroll keys reach the focused page.
key end
settle 10
assert scrolled moved
capture 02_scrolled_to_end

# ...and the offset semantics are REAL: End again at the end is an honest
# no-op, not a method that always claims it scrolled.
key end
settle 5
assert scrolled still

# Home returns to the top.
key home
settle 10
assert scrolled moved
capture 03_back_to_top

# Escape blurs back to the canvas.
key escape
settle 5
assert focus canvas

log content keyboard input receipt complete
